<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marco Polo Bridge Incident</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lugou Bridge Incident · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugou-bridge">Marco Polo Bridge</a> Incident was a clash between Chinese and Japanese troops near the Lugou Bridge south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> on the night of 7 July 1937. Fighting spread after negotiations failed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> sent reinforcements to north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The incident is generally taken as the start of the full-scale <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a>, which merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marco-polo-bridge-incident.jpg" alt="Marco Polo Bridge Incident" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sweeper tamonten · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marco_Polo_Bridge_air_view.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
